{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "rates-evap-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.48: `rates-evap`, the Rates-scale twin of `process-evap-permeation`, `process-evap-fvv`, `process-evap-leaks` and `process-refueling` together -- THC from permeation (11), fuel vapor venting (12) and leaks (13), and from refueling displacement (18) and spillage (19), for the gasoline-selected passenger car in Washtenaw County on road types 1 and 4 (all five on-network road types in MOVES's execution `runspecroadtype`), at `<modelscale value=\"Rates\"/>`. MOVES writes THC only: TOG and VOC, which the XML also names, are not in the Rates tables.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. (1) The EVAPORATIVE on-road rows: RatePerDistance is MOVESOutput over the link's distance, and an evaporative rate is per source hour, so the rate per mile is the hourly rate -- the inventory's adjusted rate over the cohort's share -- over the bin speed. Measured, `ratePerDistance x avgBinSpeed` is the same at every bin and road type, and is the inventory twins' quantity over the cohort's SHO per real day. (2) REFUELING per bin, chained from running energy (`rtRate_chained`). (3) The energy PREREQUISITES refueling adds -- running and start Total Energy -- which the inventory output strips and the Rates tables keep: RatePerDistance's 91/1 rows on every road type and RatePerStart's 104 91/2 rows. (4) The off-network evaporative and refueling rows on road type 1: RatePerVehicle's permeation, leaks, displacement and spillage, over SHP as the link's SourceHours, TTG-6's computed soak fractions and refueling's road-1 energy parents (part C1 of §7.3.48); and RatePerProfile's vapor venting on road type 1 (C2).\n\nTHE BINDINGS. `n_ratesScale` = 1 and `n_outputRate` the (pollutant-process, road type, cohort) pairs, checked by `rateSurvivorCount`.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES THAT NOTHING ELSE DOES. Vapor venting on road type 1 in a run of ONE hour: its mode-151 rate is the multiday cold-soak insert (MultidayTankVaporVentingCalculator.sql TVV-3 to TVV-7), which pairs a cold-soak hour with an earlier one of the same day among the hours the worker extracts, so here it is exactly 0 -- measured in pandas before the port, all 64 RatePerProfile rows at 7.4e-06 -- and the model computes that insert, which `rates-venting` checks where it is not zero (PLAN.md §7.3.49). Reproduces as of 2026-11-01 (PLAN.md §7.3.48 part C2): RatePerDistance 31,165 of 31,165 at 1.163e-05, RatePerStart 104 of 104 at 4.9e-06, RatePerVehicle 296 of 296 at 9.068e-06, RatePerProfile 64 of 64 at 8.999e-06, StartsPerVehicle 125 of 125 at 1.0e-05, RatePerHour empty and nothing emitted.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "rates",
      "rates-evap"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-evap/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020. The scope comes from these tables and never from the RunSpec XML, whose @key attributes are 0-based indices into sorted ID lists (docs/mixed-onroad.md §0.1).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecmonth": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-evap/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecmonth.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecmonth"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, monthID 8. A key of the thermal chain and not only an axis: TTG-1 starts from `zoneMonthHour` at this month, and the cold-soak tank temperature it produces is every cold trip's key-on temperature and three degrees below where every hot soak ends.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspechour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-evap/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspechour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, hourID 7. The hour TTG-5 averages over: each trip contributes at most one segment and one soak slice to it, because no national trip spans more than 22 hours.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_aggregationhour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-evap/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_aggregationhour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "The hours the run aggregates over. This run does not set `aggregateBy`, so it is `runspechour` itself and the same file.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/rates-evap/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspechourday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecday"
      },
